| !Run for !GLWindow, example 2 of the riscos-mesa devkit.
| Lines starting with | are comments.
|
| The program is a static ELF file (everything it needs is inside it),
| but it relies on two modules that RISC OS loads from !System: UnixLib's
| SharedUnixLibrary and ARMEABISupport (both from PackMan). RMEnsure
| loads each one if it isn't already running, and stops with a clear
| message if it can't be found, rather than letting the program crash.
Set GLWindow$Dir <Obey$Dir>
RMEnsure SharedUnixLibrary 1.16 RMLoad System:Modules.SharedULib
RMEnsure SharedUnixLibrary 1.16 Error !GLWindow needs SharedUnixLibrary 1.16 or later (from PackMan)
RMEnsure ARMEABISupport 0.00 RMLoad System:Modules.ARMEABISupport
RMEnsure ARMEABISupport 0.00 Error !GLWindow needs ARMEABISupport (from PackMan)
| The hardware overlay in the program's menu needs the VideoOverlay
| module (a Raspberry Pi has it in !System). Load it if it's there; the
| program runs without it, and then its frames are always plotted.
RMEnsure VideoOverlay 0.00 IfThere System:Modules.VideoOverlay Then RMLoad System:Modules.VideoOverlay
| Start the program. Always "Run" it by its full path.
Run <GLWindow$Dir>.!RunImage
